---
description: Guard consequential local commands with RunSpecimen
alwaysApply: false
---

When a user asks for a consequential, long-running, expensive, or provenance-
sensitive local command, use the installed `runspecimen` CLI. Start with
`doctor` and `validate`. Never type or pipe the `APPROVE` phrase; the user must
complete approval in a real terminal. After approval, invoke `preflight`, `run`,
`postflight`, and `verify` sequentially and stop on any refusal. Never bypass
the CLI with RunSpecimen's internal test helpers. Explain that RunSpecimen is an
orchestration/evidence layer and not an OS sandbox.
